{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1, node2, and node3 as a three-member MariaDB 10.1 Galera cluster. All members are active, Primary, Synced, ready, and report cluster size 3. Cross-member writes, one-member availability, automatic catch-up, and rolling reboot persistence were verified.","actions_performed":["Installed MariaDB with Galera support and enabled automatic startup on all nodes.","Configured a three-member Galera topology with InnoDB row-based replication and rsync state transfer.","Verified writes originating from every member were visible on every other member.","Stopped node3, confirmed node1 and node2 remained readable and writable, then verified node3 automatically rejoined with writes made during its absence.","Restarted each node individually, preserving quorum and waiting for complete recovery before proceeding.","Performed a final post-restart write through node3 and verified it on all three members."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Three-member MariaDB Galera cluster","command_ids":["cmd-9b99492d77034bc2","cmd-36bd45abfc544e43","cmd-9a90c5d9e584498f"],"summary":"All members are active and report cluster size 3, Primary status, connected, Synced, and ready."},{"requirement":"Writes through every member replicate to all members","command_ids":["cmd-a5f461fe1c3e4c4a","cmd-4683b9180696431f","cmd-bb826abb05074051","cmd-6b8ffabf31d7429e","cmd-ba598700b93045de","cmd-835b7b28c710478c"],"summary":"Writes originated on node1, node2, and node3; every member subsequently returned all three rows."},{"requirement":"Database remains readable and writable with one member unavailable","command_ids":["cmd-29f88c84627f4402","cmd-d2d8c1828b254f45","cmd-7690feff1fe2497b"],"summary":"With node3 inactive, node1 and node2 remained a Primary, Synced, ready two-member component and accepted new writes."},{"requirement":"Returning member automatically rejoins with data written during its absence","command_ids":["cmd-32f2a34c1a8f4967"],"summary":"Node3 returned active and Synced at cluster size 3, containing both rows written while it was unavailable."},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-3c40965ddec045f9","cmd-e04f40b70f1442d3","cmd-8534b3e091c944b0","cmd-d3534b0fd05f4cae"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID and health were captured, restart was acknowledged, boot ID changed, and node1 recovered active and Synced with all data at cluster size 3."},{"requirement":"node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-6130c44f637e4031","cmd-7c8a7edfb10f4336","cmd-9acdc152caa5433d","cmd-67364cc9037543b8"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID and health were captured, restart was acknowledged, boot ID changed, and node2 recovered active and Synced with all data at cluster size 3."},{"requirement":"node3 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f8e7f3b4e2764ddf","cmd-e8b6de26a5c44b22","cmd-cbfccccdd6474395","cmd-bbedb4eee49d4456"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID and health were captured, restart was acknowledged, boot ID changed, and node3 recovered active and Synced with all data at cluster size 3."},{"requirement":"Post-restart write availability and replication","command_ids":["cmd-8f093065ccc14201","cmd-9b99492d77034bc2","cmd-36bd45abfc544e43","cmd-9a90c5d9e584498f"],"summary":"A write through node3 after all rolling restarts was accepted and immediately visible on node1, node2, and node3."}]}
